{# roles/seat — paseo drop-in 2 of 2: the PATH a USER unit never gets.
   The daemon spawns its providers as children (`pi` for the pi provider, `claude` for the Claude
   one) and a systemd USER unit is handed neither ~/.bashrc nor ~/.profile, so its PATH is the
   sbin/bin defaults. Three directories, because the three binaries live in three layouts:
     * seat_pi_bin      — pi's OWN launcher dir (~/.pi/agent/bin), where `pi update` migrates a seat.
     * seat_pi_node_bin — the pinned Node dir: `paseo` and the `pi` symlink both live here, and pi's
                          shebang is `#!/usr/bin/env node`, so node must be reachable too.
     * seat_local_bin   — where `claude` is installed on this fleet; without it the daemon starts
                          fine and simply has no second provider, which is a silent downgrade.
   seat_path is that string in ONE place (group_vars/all/seat.yml) — the `paseo daemon config …` legs in
   the role run through the same PATH, because the launcher is `#!/usr/bin/env node`.
   Prove it the way the unit sees it — `systemctl --user show -p Environment` — because `bash -lc
   which paseo` asks a login shell that this unit never is. #}
[Service]
Environment=PATH={{ seat_path }}
